  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Family Kitchen Table",
    "overview": "The site should feel like a table set by someone who cooks for you: warm cream paper, white plates (cards), burgundy and olive from the logo, and a thin marigold line under the header. Everything is rounded and soft. Nothing looks corporate, glossy or cold. It is warm and homemade, and it stays quick to use on a phone.\n\nDensity is moderate: a product grid with generous 16px gutters, one clear action per card, and a floating order bar. Expression comes from the palette, the rounded forms and the friendly Bricolage Grotesque titles, not from decoration. The client's colors and fonts live in `config.json`; this document records the PBC values currently configured.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream page, white cards, cocoa-brown ink (never pure black on pure white).",
      "Burgundy for \"add to cart\", olive for \"send the order\" and navigation chips.",
      "Pills and 16px-rounded cards; soft, low shadows.",
      "Bricolage Grotesque for titles, Figtree for everything else.",
      "Emoji stand in when a product has no photo."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two-Verb Rule",
        "body": "Burgundy means \"put this in my order\"; olive means \"send it / go there\". A button of the wrong color confuses the flow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Whisper Rule",
        "body": "Marigold appears only as a thin line, never as a surface. Its rarity is the point.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Titles Rule",
        "body": "Section titles and headings use Cocoa Ink; color is reserved for actions.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Amounts in the cotizador use tabular numerals so columns of pesos align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Float-Means-Action Rule",
        "body": "Only things that follow the visitor (the order bar, the sticky category bar) or interrupt them (the dialog) get strong depth. Content stays calm.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use Cellar Burgundy to add an item and Olive Grove to send or navigate.",
      "**Do** keep cream as the page background and white for surfaces that hold content.",
      "**Do** keep every tappable control at least 34px, and prefer 40px for header icons.",
      "**Do** read colors and fonts from the `config.json` variables (`--principal`, `--secundario`, `--acento`, `--fondo`, `--tinta`...), never hard-coded hex.",
      "**Do** keep working when a product has no photo, no price or is out of stock."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace the established identity (logo, burgundy / olive / gold on cream, «Hecho con amor»); this is a confirmed commitment.",
      "**Don't** use marigold as a fill or for text.",
      "**Don't** color titles; they stay Cocoa Ink.",
      "**Don't** crop product photos or add decorative imagery that competes with them.",
      "**Don't** add pure black text or cold gray surfaces."
    ]
  }
}
